<text use-page-width="false" push-down="false" lock-width="true"><p style="Normal" margin-left="inherit" margin-right="inherit" text-indent="inherit" text-align="inherit" list-style-type="inherit" tabs="inherit">Stations k: 0 = S, the shear-governing point; 1, 2, 3 = N, P, B, the longitudinal-tension points of each region; 4 = M, the least minimum transverse steel. Each line gives the interval, combination C, element E, load state, station and tension face; the equations recompute every check there.</p></text>
</region>
